.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt INITFSD 8
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm initfsd
.Nd RavenBSD read-only filesystem server over the initfs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
maps the initfs MemObject at handle 1, validates it once with the
.Sy raven-initfs
reader and registers the
.Dq initfs:
scheme.
It synthesises a directory tree from the sorted initfs paths: every prefix is a directory with mode
0755 and files keep their archive mode.
.Pp
The server is strictly read-only.
.Dv OPEN
with
.Dv WRITE
or
.Dv CREATE
returns
.Er EROFS
and every mutating
.Dv CALL
operation returns
.Er EROFS .
Only
.Dv STATFS
is accepted through
.Dv CALL .
.Pp
.Dv READ
of a file copies bytes at the requested offset and returns a short read at end of file.
.Dv READ
of a directory returns packed K60 directory entries in sorted order without
.Pa .
or
.Pa .. .
.Dv FSTAT
reports the file size and archive mode, inode numbers (entry index plus one for files), link count
one for files and two for directories, and zero timestamps.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/services.d -compact
.It Pa /etc/services.d/initfsd.toml
Service manifest; it sets the environment variable
.Dv INITFS_HANDLE=1 .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr init 8 ,
.Xr ramfsd 8
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
